/**
	The pitch of the voice, from -10 (lowest) to 10 (highest), with 0 being the default.
	float tts_voice::pitch;
	## Remarks:
		Values outside the range are clamped to it. Until it is assigned, it reports the pitch the engine starts with, which may not be 0; see pitch_set for what that is on each platform. With Speech Dispatcher on Linux, which uses its own configuration, it reports 0 until assigned, and assigning it doesn't change the speech. This is the property form of set_pitch and get_pitch.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	v.pitch = 5;
	v.speak_wait("This is spoken at a higher pitch.");
	v.pitch = -5;
	v.speak_wait("And this at a lower one.");
}
